INT. LISTENING POST, CHALK TUNNEL UNDER A COASTAL RIDGE - NIGHT

A narrow chalk-white tunnel shored with timber. Hurricane lamps hang from nails. At a plank table, a radio set glows green, headphones draped over its dial. The sea is a dull pulse in the rock.

CAPTAIN ELSPETH MORRIGAN-ADEWALE (40s, wool greatcoat, tin mug between both palms) sits with her back to the wall, eyes on the radio. Opposite her, a field cot, and on it LIEUTENANT BASTIAN OKOYE-LINDGREN (20s, collar open, a letter half-written on his knee). A third man, SERGEANT AUGUSTIN "GUS" PELLETIER-ONUOHA (30s, signal corps, headphones on), is bent over the set with a pencil.

For an hour nothing has come over the wire. The three of them have the look of people who have stopped expecting it to.

ELSPETH
Gus, anything?

GUS
Static, ma'am.

ELSPETH
Same static as before?

GUS
Same. Pretty one.

BASTIAN
Pretty static. I'll tell Mother.

ELSPETH
Lieutenant, the letter.

BASTIAN
Captain?

ELSPETH
Don't write that last page until morning.

He looks at her. Folds the page once, and tucks it into his breast pocket with ceremony.

BASTIAN
Yes, ma'am.

The radio gives a click. A long, dry hiss. Gus freezes, one finger raised. Elspeth sets down her mug without making a sound.

COMMANDER (V.O.)
(through the headphones, loud enough to leak)
Hawk Nest, Hawk Nest, this is Tower. Do you read?

GUS
(into mic)
Tower, Hawk Nest. Loud and clear.

COMMANDER (V.O.)
Hawk Nest, stand by for orders.

GUS
(to Elspeth)
Orders, ma'am.

ELSPETH
I heard.

She stands, takes the headphones from Gus, and settles them on her ears.

ELSPETH (CONT'D)
(into mic)
Tower, Hawk Nest. Captain Morrigan-Adewale speaking.

COMMANDER (V.O.)
Captain, the ridge is to be vacated by oh-four-hundred.

ELSPETH
(a beat)
Repeat, Tower?

COMMANDER (V.O.)
Vacate by oh-four-hundred. Demolition charges on the tunnel mouth. Acknowledge.

Silence. Gus looks at Bastian. Bastian looks at Elspeth.

ELSPETH
(into mic)
Tower, we have a signal watch of seven hours remaining.

COMMANDER (V.O.)
Captain, the watch is cancelled. The enemy has taken the eastern shore.

BASTIAN
(whispering)
But it's calm.

GUS
(whispering)
Too calm.

ELSPETH
(into mic)
Understood, Tower. Hawk Nest will withdraw.

She pulls the headphones off. The tunnel is quiet. The sea thumps against the cliff, faint, constant.

ELSPETH (CONT'D)
(to the room)
Gentlemen. Pack the set. Leave the tin.

GUS
Ma'am, the tin has the codebooks.

ELSPETH
Then burn the codebooks first.

BASTIAN
And the letters?

ELSPETH
Take your letters.

Bastian hesitates. Takes his letter from his pocket. Holds it out to her.

BASTIAN
Captain, would you post it?

ELSPETH
I'll try.

BASTIAN
(together)
Thank you.

GUS ^
(together)
Thank you.

Both stop. Gus looks at his pencil. Bastian looks at his boots.

ELSPETH
Let's go.

She takes the lamp from its nail, and the three of them step into the dark of the tunnel mouth, where, beyond the ridge, a faint red line is beginning to rise out of the sea.
